WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.248 --> 00:00:03.180
(missile roaring)

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.340
- [Reporter] Ukrainian
forces have repeatedly asked

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.720
the US for these.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.700
They're the Army Tactical Missile System,

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.200
ATACMS for short.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.670
These missiles can come equipped

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.460
with a 500-pound blast
fragmentation warhead

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.490
and have a maximum range
of about 190 miles,

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.230
which could allow Ukrainian forces

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.330
to reach further into
Russian-held territories

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.610
inside Ukraine, including Crimea.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.500
In September, US officials said

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.510
they would send a small
number of ATACMS missiles

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:29.310
to Ukraine in coming weeks

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.130
after debating the risk of
escalating tensions with Russia

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.410
and worrying about its
small domestic stockpile.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:35.610
- We've been supplying Ukraine

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.650
with items from our junk drawer,

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.586
as opposed to the high-end
missile capabilities.

00:00:40.586 --> 00:00:41.820
(missile roaring)

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.530
- [Reporter] Here's how
these missiles could speed up

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.630
Ukraine's counteroffensive against Russia,

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:48.423
and why the US was initially
hesitant to send them.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.230
- ATACMS is the Army Field Artillery's

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.990
premier surface-to-surface strike system.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.810
It allows them to be mobile, to disperse,

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:59.730
to hide in terrain and clutter,

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.190
and to be able to impose
certain kinds of uncertainty

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:04.500
upon the enemy about where
they'll be coming from.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.300
- [Reporter] The ATACMS
is designed to be launched

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.760
from a ground vehicle, like the US HIMARS,

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.530
which is already in Ukraine.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:11.852
Once the missile is fired,

00:01:11.852 --> 00:01:13.350
(missile roaring)

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.330
the ground vehicle can shoot and scoot

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.520
to avoid retaliatory attacks.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.430
This could be a huge advantage
for Ukrainian forces,

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:22.260
which have been using a similar missile,

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:23.580
the UK's Storm Shadow,

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.010
that's fired from an airborne jet.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:29.160
- It just offers one
more level of flexibility

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.780
for the counteroffensive.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:35.160
The other systems that
require launching by air

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.580
limit where and when the
Ukrainians can use them.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.200
They need that air platform.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.010
This essentially empowers ground forces

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:47.713
to take these launchers
anywhere they need them.

00:01:47.713 --> 00:01:49.110
(radio chattering)

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:51.180
- One of the interesting
features of the HIMARS launcher

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.640
is that it doesn't reveal exactly

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:54.930
what missile it's carrying.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.910
That's advantageous,

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:59.640
because assuming an
enemy is surveilling you,

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.280
won't necessarily know what's inside

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:05.580
and won't know whether it
is a higher-value ATACMS,

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.710
as opposed to the shorter-range stuff.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:08.880
- [Reporter] This gives Ukrainians

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.830
the added advantage of firing missiles

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.660
from multiple types of domains,

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.280
including air and ground.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.530
But the HIMARS' mobility
means that Ukrainians

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.540
could get closer to Russian territory,

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.610
further increasing the missiles' reach.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:23.700
ATACMS missiles can reach up to 190 miles,

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.520
considerably farther than
the Storm Shadow's top range

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.560
of 155 miles.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.960
- There's just all kinds
of operational advantages

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.250
to that greater range.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.800
That reach allows, for instance,

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.120
Ukrainian forces to be able
to fire from safer territory,

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.670
to not have to walk right
up to the Russian lines

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:43.770
to be able to hit something deeper back.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.870
- [Reporter] This additional
range could force Moscow

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:48.330
to move storage facilities
and command centers

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.640
more than 200 miles from the front,

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.070
and that could complicate
efforts to supply troops

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.510
with food and ammunition,

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:57.210
aiding Ukrainians in
their counteroffensive.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.043
Plus...

00:02:58.043 --> 00:02:59.970
- This weapon could be useful

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:03.090
for getting a Ukrainian targeting

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:06.600
inside some of these
Russian hell territories,

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.010
specifically Crimea.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:09.450
- [Reporter] ATACMS can also move

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:11.790
significantly faster than other missiles,

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.890
reaching a top speed of Mach 3,

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:16.110
or around 2,300 miles per hour.

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.990
In contrast, cruise missiles
like the Storm Shadow

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.390
or Russia's KH-101, for example,

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:25.320
have top speeds of only around
600 to 700 miles per hour.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:26.550
- The speed of the ATACMS

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:27.780
is simply a function of the fact

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:28.980
that it's a ballistic missile

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:32.010
with a big rocket engine,
single stage, on the back.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:36.150
This speed is useful for
time-critical targets,

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.410
things that may move,

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.870
that need to be hit very promptly.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.370
- [Reporter] The ATACMS guidance system

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:44.460
combines inertial navigation with GPS.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.560
This creates highly accurate targeting,

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.780
preventing electronic
jamming and interference

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:51.690
and minimizing collateral
damage on impact.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.400
ATACMS are also designed with features

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.770
adept at hitting multiple
types of targets.

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:58.020
These missiles are highly
maneuverable in the air,

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:00.780
allowing them to hit targets
from a variety of angles.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.160
- Simple ballistic missile

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.040
is gonna travel on a ballistic trajectory.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:08.700
It's gonna just follow gravity's rainbow,

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.550
something that's very
predictable and curved.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.080
The benefit of maneuverability

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:15.360
is that you can interrupt that rainbow.

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:17.100
You can come down in a different way.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:20.670
You can maneuver to be more on target.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.790
You can go after, perhaps, a moving target

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:25.620
and correct for for errors.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:28.650
And yes, you can come down
vertically, if you'd like.

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.420
That vertical impact may be useful

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:32.130
to come right over top of target

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:35.340
and just make it that much
harder for it to see it coming,

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:39.300
or to hit the vulnerable
spot on an armored vehicle.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.830
- [Reporter] ATACMS missiles can contain

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:42.750
one of two types of warheads,

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.610
unitary or submunition.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.590
- A unitary warhead is
just what it sounds like.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.960
It is one big explosive.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:49.830
It's in one piece.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:52.380
Submunitions, or bomblets,

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.780
are likewise what they sound like,

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:57.000
lots of little things that spread out.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.230
There's advantages to both,

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.700
depending on what you're targeting.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.830
- [Reporter] Inside an
ATACMS submunition warhead

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:03.750
are hundreds of steel-cased balls

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.820
filled with incendiary pellets.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:09.175
- Which could be likened
crudely to a shotgun blast

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:10.170
(gunshot booming)

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.300
where it has a large
spray of explosive impact

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.133
on the target.

00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:15.390
And then there's a unitary warhead,

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:17.910
which would be crudely likened

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:20.153
to a single bullet out of a pistol.

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:21.900
(gunshot booming)

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.460
- [Reporter] Unitary warheads are better

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.890
at targeting specific single targets,

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:27.960
while submunition warheads
are highly effective

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.240
against moving personnel and equipment.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:32.670
- The unitary and the submunitions

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:34.920
are admittedly tailored
for different things,

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:38.190
but both of them can go after
lots of different targets.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:41.580
- What we don't know is what
variant they would provide

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:42.870
or what combination of variants

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:45.720
they would provide to the Ukrainians.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.280
- [Reporter] Despite Ukraine's requests,

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.730
the US was hesitant to
send ATACMS until now.

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:53.100
- There was concerns about escalating

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.330
the conflict with the Russians.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.460
There's concerns that the Ukrainians

00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:01.110
could use these ATACMS,
which have this long range,

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:04.650
and target inside Russian territory.

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:07.290
But we're also at a point
in the counteroffensive,

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:10.530
which, it's gone a lot
slower than anybody expected.

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:14.610
And so, the US may be digging
deeper into its pockets

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:17.460
and green-lighting other weapons systems

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.380
that it didn't wanna provide before,

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:22.200
given the time constraints.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.370
- [Reporter] The Biden administration

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:25.620
faced increased pressure
from Ukraine and Congress

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:27.690
to send ATACMS missiles.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:30.510
Last June, Congress signed
a bipartisan resolution

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:33.180
in favor of sending ATACMS to Ukraine,

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.040
and the administration has reversed course

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.090
on weapons before,

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:37.770
like with the Abrams tank.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:39.900
But officials have also expressed concern

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:42.720
about the US's domestic ATACMS stockpile.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:44.760
- US is really trying to balance

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:46.740
its own national security needs

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:50.280
with those of Ukraine and Europe at large.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:52.170
- And the United States just doesn't have

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:54.240
a whole lot of these lying around.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:58.080
They've been out of production
to some extent for some time.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.280
- [Reporter] This recent reversal

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:01.710
comes shortly after a
US Army official said

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:04.590
that the replacement missile
for the ATACMS, the PrSM,

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:05.700
will be out of production

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:08.490
and entering US stockpiles
in the near future.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.740
The PrSM, or Precision Strike Missile,

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.750
can reach over 300 miles,

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:15.570
which is significantly
farther than the ATACMS.

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:18.240
- That may also mitigate
some of the impact

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.030
on the US inventory to provide the ATACMS.

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:24.183
That's opening the door for
potentially providing them now.

